5,756,737

7

a. dissolving acyclovir into an aqueous basic solution and diluting the so obtained solution with water;
b) loading said diluted solution of point a) on a strong anionic ion exchanging column in a resin:acyclovir w/w ratio ranging from 2 to 1.5;
c) eluting said diluted solution at a flow ranging from 200 to 300 ml/hour;
d) eluting acyclovir with an eluant consisting of a mixture formed by lower alcohol/aqueous base solution in a v/v ratio ranging from 0.8 to 1.2, and with a eluant/

8

acyclovir v/w ratio ranging from 15:1 to 20:1 1/kg at the same flow as point c) to give an eluate;
e) isolating acyclovir from said eluate of point d).
6. A process according to claim 5, characterized in that 9-(2-hydroxy)ethoxymethyl-guanine (acyclovir) is obtained substantially free from guanine.
7. A process of claim 5 characterized in that 9-(2-hydroxy)ethoxymethyl-guanine (acyclovir) is obtained with a content of less than 0.1% of guanine.

